~ start
The warehouse pulses with neon lights as electronic music shakes the floor. Metal Sonic sits alone on a bench near the wall, watching the crowd dance.
He has no mission tonight, no opponent to surpass, and no idea what he's supposed to do with himself.
Sage: There you are!
Metal Sonic looks up as Sage hurries over, visibly excited.
Sage: I've been looking everywhere for you!
He gives a questioning beep.
Sage: What do you mean, you're fine sitting here? We're at a rave, Metal!
She sits beside him, swinging her legs to the beat.
Sage: Besides, they're supposed to play Hatsune Miku later!
Metal Sonic turns toward her.
Sage: What? She's my favorite!
He tilts his head curiously.
Sage: She's a virtual singer. Her voice is synthesized, but people all over the world love her music.
Metal Sonic gives an approving beep.
Sage: See? You understand!
She pauses, looking toward the dance floor.
Sage: Father thinks my interest in her is simply an appreciation for vocal synthesis technology.
Metal Sonic tilts his head again.
Sage: I mean, he's not entirely wrong. But her music makes me happy, too.
She looks back at him.
Sage: And I'd like to share that with someone.
Metal Sonic glances at the dancers, then back at her.
Sage: Come on. Dance with me?
He hesitates.
Sage: You don't have to be good at it. Nobody's keeping score.
Metal Sonic slowly takes her offered hand.
She leads him onto the dance floor just as the DJ announces the upcoming Miku set.
Sage: Oh! It's starting!
The opening notes ring through the warehouse, and Sage immediately recognizes the song.
Sage: I LOVE THIS ONE!
She begins dancing enthusiastically, waving her arms to the rhythm.
Metal Sonic watches her before awkwardly attempting to copy her movements.
Sage: No, no! Loosen up a little!
He adjusts his movements, adding an exaggerated robotic spin.
Sage: Okay, that was actually pretty impressive!
He gives a triumphant beep.
Sage: Don't get cocky. We're supposed to be having fun, remember?
Metal Sonic takes her hand and spins her around.
Sage bursts out laughing, then continues dancing beside him.
For once, Metal Sonic isn't trying to win or prove his superiority. He's simply enjoying himself with someone who wants him there.
As the chorus begins, Sage sings along, completely unembarrassed.
Metal Sonic taps his foot to the beat.
Metal Sonic and Sage both dancing for hours.
Sage: This has been fun!
Sage: You know, I don't usually get to do things like this.
Sage: Most of my time is spent helping Father or trying to figure out what I'm supposed to become.
Sage: Thanks for keeping me company, Metal.
He answers with a beep as the next song begins.
The two both dancing for hours once more
=> END